The first books make an entrance available. Research requires a defensible Greek text, its editorial evidence, sustained scholarship, and the current debate relevant to a precise question.

| Role | References |
| --- | --- |
| Greek text and apparatus | [Plato](Plato-critical-editions.lingua#r_28N1ADM4R3DAG5K2898WPKRXCK); [Aristotle's Metaphysics](Metaphysics-Jaeger.lingua#r_2MJF84NGSE83J9KWD3B8KBNPZ1); [Plotinus](Plotinus-Henry-Schwyzer.lingua#r_3EYTA95ETXPPZFHSN5RJ5Q5EM4) |
| Grammar and textual preparation | [Smyth, 1920](Greek-Grammar-Smyth.lingua#r_1HWQDW2XAJNQAXTWS9P0QT57DG); [Peek's first course](Ancient-Greek-Peek.lingua#r_1D87YRHMAM7FHZH3VCDY9JTHGX); [the Greek dossier](../research/Philological-study.lingua#r_353E4E4WH3BWFHHJNZMPKBPEXF) |
| Earlier Greek evidence | [Kirk, Raven, and Schofield](Presocratics-Kirk-Raven-Schofield.lingua#r_13P4W9K1D0PTV3VCEPQEXQNVSM), compared with the existing collections and the transmitting passages |
| Plato and interpretive disputes | [Sophist](Sophist-Jowett.lingua#r_4B67CBBBRAQS5SCS5M5K8RGXXR); [Cordero](Sophist-Cordero.lingua#r_5MPQY66DGXV4RRE8GCWCCKJ952); [Levett/Burnyeat/Williams](Theaetetus-Levett-Burnyeat.lingua#r_615423T7F74G6W17SFHWMSMDV9); [Merker](Desire-Merker.lingua#r_4VJ745X9FCY3MY2FB5G9KKA0GC) |
| Aristotle and sustained interpretation | [Loux on substance](Primary-Ousia-Loux.lingua#r_1T3SW7QAK4FKG98YMZ6J83F28J); [Broadie on ethics](Ethics-Broadie.lingua#r_5W2X8XTJ2MP72E74E1CR3EGPC9); [On the Soul](On-the-Soul-Smith.lingua#r_3RK7WZ5X419B2RJGCK5E7K15TE) |
| Hellenistic sources and notes | [Long and Sedley, both volumes](Hellenistic-Philosophers-Long-Sedley.lingua#r_0DRQW2CEH35TV91C49W4JH7Y0M) |
| Later Platonism | [The Six Enneads](Enneads-MacKenna-Page.lingua#r_1Q1GRWKVQMEPBGQH3V7WR9RQP8); [Gerson](Plotinus-Gerson.lingua#r_170Z1XNEHXR1V514CP6AEC0NXB); the corresponding Greek critical text |
| Evidence for depth and scope | [University courses, programme descriptors, and research outputs](Academic-benchmarks.lingua#r_7YDPSHERTRH41D7YR4P93PWNEP) |

These are starting references for problem-specific research. A classic commentary remains a position to examine; the [literature dossier](../research/Scholarly-inquiry.lingua#r_2FEBDJ8R5JDHXX54TSATY2CRVZ) must locate relevant later contributions and serious alternatives. Comparable scholarship can replace a suggested work when the replacement's role and depth are justified.

The Sophist EPUB is retained locally. Other entries here are external texts, historical digitisations, journal references, or publisher/library editions unless their source Record declares a retained artifact. Obtain the selected edition through its stated access and preserve its attribution and reuse terms. A preview or catalogue establishes metadata, not a claim to have read the book.

